---
description: Git commits are made by the user, never by the agent
alwaysApply: true
---

# Human Commits Only

Only the user creates git commits in this project. The agent prepares code; the user lands it.

- Do not run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, `git push`, or create commits on behalf of the user unless they explicitly ask you to commit.
- Do not stage files (`git add`) in preparation for a commit unless the user explicitly asks for staging help without committing.
- Do not create empty commits when there are no changes.
- When work is ready to land, summarize the diff and let the user commit manually.
- If the user asks to "save" or "finish" work, treat that as code completion — not permission to commit.
- Only discuss commit messages or git workflow when the user brings up committing themselves.
